> We will go deeper later when we study gradient behavior and activation sparsity. For now, a strong mental model is more than enough.

@section how-to-use-this-guide | How to use this guide
## This is a sequential course, it builds up.

The main text is the course. Videos, papers, and demonstrations deepen a point, but modules won't be standalone units, they will rely on previous material.
::component Steps
{
  "items": [
    {
      "title": "Read once for the shape",
      "description": "Build the high-level model, glossing over derivation."
    },
    {
      "title": "Re-examine the details when comfortable",
      "description": "Not every derivation or idea is obvious, take your time when needed."
    },
    {
      "title": "Dive deeper",
      "description": "Use the linked ressources off your own initiative to get a deeper view on a specific idea."
    }
  ]
}
::end

